From fa2a8108136de608dce5b9c5094d05f432cda6d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: avdim <avdimdv@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 19:45:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] chagall-common: fingerprint: fix leaks, hangs, a crash and
 enrol/remove reporting

The Validity fingerprint HAL captured fine but unlocking never worked,
deleting a fingerprint never refreshed Settings, and a 60 s enrolment
timeout could hang the HAL and put system_server into a watchdog restart
loop. Measured on an SM-T800:

- vcs_uninit() leaked the 128 KB secure ion buffer (mmap, ion handle,
  /dev/ion, /dev/s5p-smem) on every session. That filled the whole
  "secdma" region (exactly 0x20000), so every later ion_alloc_fd failed
  with ENOMEM and the HAL only limped on by reusing the first session's
  stale fd. Free it; vcs_init() fails cleanly if allocation fails, and the
  start functions reset the state on any setup failure.
- vfmEnrollFinish was checked against vfmVendorDefinedOperationRsp instead
  of vfmEnrollFinishRsp, so every enrolment logged an error and carried on.
  A real failure now reports UNABLE_TO_PROCESS and stores nothing.
  vfmPayloadBind's second call answers rc=5 here; the template is kept with
  a warning (the payload is only released after a successful match). Enrol
  error exits now close the secure session instead of returning early.
- vcs_timeout() set STATE_CANCEL but never woke the capture thread, which
  sleeps on sensor.cond until DRDY. Its wait loop spun forever, the next
  cancel() blocked in pthread_join() on it, and system_server's watchdog
  restarted the framework over and over. Wake the thread; every wait for
  the worker is bounded (3 s) so the HAL can no longer block a binder call
  forever.
- The worker went to STATE_IDLE before closing its sessions, so a request
  arriving right after a cancel found "TA already running", used half-freed
  state and crashed (SIGSEGV in vcs_authenticate), or was refused as busy.
  New STATE_EXIT: only vcs_uninit() sets STATE_IDLE, after everything is
  closed; new requests wait up to 1 s for a session that is winding down.
- send_remove_notice() left gid and remaining_templates uninitialised
  (seen: gid=6, rem=69960371), so the framework's removal never completed.
- The template table was cleared one slot short when reloading.
- FPDBG step trace (ALOGV, off by default) for every secure-world command.

With a clean template database this enrols and unlocks;
vfmMatchImageToTemplates answers 601 for a swipe that does not match well
enough.

Change-Id: Ifcd324f048725df1ebd66559dae564687c5d952d
